# Mirror utensil hygiene (operator-local)

**`~/coding/hapi` (primary mirror) must stay clean enough for any agent to sync + rematerialize soup.**

Dirty `package.json` / lockfiles / untracked `e2e/` on the mirror block `hapi-sync-fork-main` and `hapi-driver-rebuild` for everyone. That is a kitchen-skunk failure, not a private WIP choice.

## NEVER on the mirror

- `bun install` / `npm install` / `pnpm` / `yarn` / `bun add` at `~/coding/hapi`
- Write `e2e/**`, `package.json`, or lockfiles on the mirror for feature / peer e2e work

## ALWAYS use a worktree instead

```bash
cd ~/coding/hapi/worktrees/<your-feature>
bun install          # OK here
# write e2e specs here
```

## Mechanical guard

`scripts/tooling/hapi-mirror-hygiene-guard.sh` (Cursor + Claude PreToolUse) denies the NEVER list. Install/refresh: `scripts/tooling/hapi-install-cursor-hooks.sh`.

Bypass (operator TTY only): `HAPI_OPERATOR_MIRROR_HYGIENE_OVERRIDE=1`

## Allowed on mirror (not blocked by this guard)

- `docs/operator/`, `docs/plans/`, `docs/tooling/`, `scripts/tooling/`
- `config/driver-manifest.yaml` (intentional soup layer WIP — **mess-maker must commit before turn end**; see `hapi-tooling-commit-hygiene.mdc`)
- Product code is already blocked by `hapi-product-code-guard` outside worktrees

See `docs/tooling/driver-soup.md#mirror-utensil-hygiene` and mess-maker commits section.
